AB  - It is well recognised that, from time to time, local government requires the services of consultants, whatever the discipline. Their use and need is two-fold. When capacity within a council is such that it cannot handle the volume required of it, then the consultant can relieve that pressure. Secondly, the consultant brings with him the best expertise in his field, an expertise that is not always available within the council staffing. This paper looks at the use of consultants from both the council's and consultant's point of view, highlighting the difficulties experienced by both and bringing together a rationale for the better and more effective use of consultants to the benefit of the community generally.
