TY  - JOUR
TI  - 政策過程上 組織學習行態에 觀한 硏究
AU  - 韓富榮
AU  - 崔殷碩
PY  - 2000
JO  - 한국지방자치학회보
AB  - Since the late 1970s, privatization, deregulation and competition policy have become increasingly important elements in the policy mix of industrialized countries. Governments have increasingly recognized that open and efficient markets for good services, exposed to domestic and international competition, provide the crucial underpinnings for dynamic, high income economies. Contracting out program is the typical case of these reforming program. This study explores the problems of contracting out program in local government with the notion of learning. Learning, used on this study, is a concept including positive effects and negative effects on policy goal attainment. The analysis of contracting out program on solid-waste management, the misbelief in optimistic manner on the probability of success will bring about great error and damage to the program. Particularly, anti-learning behaviors on the program are connected with tragedy of the commons under the absence of quasi-learning efforts. The incentives to acquire pure knowledge are affected not only by the structure of monetary rewards and punishments, but also by social tolerances of its learning accumulation. These findings have important implications for the future of studies on policy process under ambiguity and complexity.
