TY  - JOUR
TI  - Infrastructure investments and land value capture: variations and uncertainties at the frontiers of urban expansion
AU  - Minjee Kim
PY  - 2022
JO  - Town Planning Review
AB  - Large-scale infrastructure investments create opportunities for land value capture. Nevertheless, scholars have cautioned that the calculative practices undergirding value capture tools produce neither objective nor absolute outputs. This problem is exacerbated at the frontiers of urban expansion where land markets are disrupted by public intervention. This paper analyses the case of Citrus County, Florida to examine the feasibility of land value capture when rural land is pried open by public investments. The magnitude and timing of land value uplift is estimated in this context. A significant variation within the development industry was found. Only a small group of developers foresaw profitable opportunities, where others saw none. Significant value capture opportunities are expected to arise, but only idiosyncratically and in the long run. This can pose practical challenges for designing value capture tools. The paper concludes by discussing policy implications for land value capture at the frontiers of urban expansion.
