TI  - Les transversalités contrariées de l’action publique
AU  - Vincent Lebrou
AU  - Luc Sigalo Santos
PY  - 2024
JO  - Pôle Sud
AB  - The sectoral organisation of public policies is being called into question in the name of optimized allocation of resources and better-adjusted handling of users. Under the initial impulse of the European Commission calling for ‘cross-cutting’ and ‘collaborative’ policies, systems are being developed combining several, and sometimes all, areas of public policy. However, the combined results of two ethnographic surveys carried out on territorial welfare policies reveal that such a slogan struggles to be operationalized. Crossing the sectoral boundaries of public policy is nothing obvious or automatic: it is a loosely binding instruction, the implementation of which is here thwarted by professionals from sectors who have little interest in playing the game of bureaucratic cooperation.
