AU  - CHNIGRI, Yousra
AU  - SADIK, Mohammed
AU  - SLIMANI, Hamid
PY  - 2024
JO  - Alternatives Managériales Economiques
AB  - The dynamic capabilities (DC) approach represents a new theoretical perspective which may enhance our still limited understanding of the way in which public organizations evolve in response to an increasingly turbulent and complex environment. The main aim of this study is to first identify the role that dynamic capabilities can play in public sector organizations and then to recommend further studies. As for the methodological framework, this article will provide a systematic review of the literature elaborated from the Scopus database which allows us to incorporate and analyze fourteen articles out of a total of 51 studies published between 2013 and 2022. The analysis is broken down into three groups: DC for performance, innovation and resilience. Our results reveal that this subject has received little treatment in the public context despite its contribution to an improved performance, a sustained innovation and a reinforcement of the resilience of this type of organizations. From this work, we point out new subjects for further research in the conceptual as well as in the methodological framework.
