TI  - The Iceberg Beneath the Org Chart A Framework for Navigating Informal Authority in Public-Sector Modernization
AU  - William Parris
PY  - 2026
JO  - Zenodo (CERN European Organization for Nuclear Research)
AB  - Public-sector modernization initiatives frequently fail not because the technology selected was wrong, but because the organizations implementing it had already lost the ability to hear themselves. This paper introduces a four-type typology of informal authority holders in public agencies: the Silent Fixer, the Frustrated Escalator, the Reluctant Gatekeeper, and the Network Operator. It argues that the strategic exclusion of informal knowledge holders from modernization decision-making is a governance architecture failure with measurable fiscal consequences.
